# Story 106: Viewing Shared Tabs on Mobile (45s)
# Hook: A teammate shares a tab -- you open the whole multi-pane layout on your phone.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-106-viewing-shared-tabs-mobile.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
A teammate shares a tab -- you open the whole multi-pane layout on your phone.

[00:05.0 --> 00:14.0]
It starts on the desktop: a teammate runs share tab, which publishes the tab and every pane inside it to the workspace.

[00:14.0 --> 00:25.0]
On mobile you subscribe to that share and the tab arrives as a full multi-pane layout -- not a flat list, the real arrangement of panes.

[00:25.0 --> 00:36.0]
Then you interact: read each shared pane, and if the share is in control mode, send input straight back into it from your phone.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
Shared tabs turn your phone into a live window onto a teammate's whole workspace.

